    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d566">

                <pb facs="0765" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg675"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.6331/179</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornbeck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-26">July 26, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Japanese Chargé called on me by appointment and stated that he had received
                    an account from his Government of an unfortunate incident at Mukden. He then
                    gave a narrative of the intrusion by the Japanese youth at Mukden into the
                    American Consulate General and the attempted assault upon Vice Consul
                        Hall,<anchor n="52" xml:id="d566-f1"/> at the conclusion of which he stated
                    that his Government regretted this and he wished to express his own regret. I
                    stated that we felt that the incident was very unfortunate and that I
                    appreciated his having come and having expressed regret.<anchor n="53"
                        xml:id="d566-f2"/></p>
                <p>Mr. Fujii then said that he wished to give me a memorandum<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d566-f3"/> with regard to a question of income taxes in this country
                    of Japanese shipping companies. At that point I asked whether I might have Mr.
                        Dooman<anchor n="55" xml:id="d566-f4"/> hear what Mr. Fujii had to say with
                    regard to that matter, and, with Mr. Fujii’s assent, I called Mr. Dooman in.
                    This matter is dealt with in a separate memorandum.<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d566-f5"/></p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">tanley</hi>] K. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ornbeck</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
